# STORY (Act 1 writing). Hawk's briefings, Cobra Commander's broadcast and the Act 1 cutscene captions.
# Text only. BUILD wires the ids (see story_tools/gen_act1_text.py). Generated: edit the script, not this file.
extraStrings:
- type: en-US
  strings: &id001
    STR_BRIEFING_CARTEL_RANCH_TITLE: 'OPERATION: BORDER RANCH'
    STR_BRIEFING_CARTEL_RANCH: 'HAWK: Listen up. For a year every agency in Washington has traded rumours about a new outfit: well armed, well paid, never there when anyone looks. No name. No photograph.
      So we start where the guns are.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}A cartel runs loads across the Rio Grande onto a ranch on the Texas side. Their gunmen are carrying hardware they have no business owning. I want to
      know who sold it to them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The boss keeps his books in a safe in the ranch house. Get that ledger, and don''t blow the safe: paper burns. Search the barn. Whatever came in those crates
      came from somewhere.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}There''s a tower on the north-east corner covering the airstrip. Nobody crosses open ground under that rifle. Take the boss alive if you can.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Clean
      operation, people. There are civilians on that ranch.'
    STR_BRIEFING_ABANDONED_FACTORY_TITLE: 'OPERATION: DEAD FACTORY'
    STR_BRIEFING_ABANDONED_FACTORY: 'HAWK: We pulled one thread for a month and it held all the way. The ranch, the flight, the stash house, the robbery, the bank. Every trail ends at a machine works on
      a rail spur in West Texas. It went bust two years ago and it''s still being paid.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Our information says it''s empty. Treat that as a guess. Search everything: the offices, the lockers,
      the boxcar, the furnace. I want to know who owns it, what they made, and whether they''re coming back.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Watch your feet. People who walk away from a place like that sometimes leave
      a present behind. And put somebody on the water tower.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Get what you find back to the A.P.C. and get out. We go in, we read their mail, we leave.'
    STR_BRIEFING_COBRA_CELL_TITLE: 'OPERATION: FIRST CONTACT'
    STR_BRIEFING_COBRA_CELL: 'HAWK: Now we know what they call themselves. Breaker pulled Cobra Commander''s broadcast apart. It bounced through three relays, and the first one was sloppy. It leads to one
      building with a Cobra cell in it.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Don''t get excited. This is not their headquarters. A cell is a few rooms, a radio, and people who take orders. That''s what we want: the people.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Every
      one of them knows a name we don''t. Bring me a Cobra soldier alive and Scarlett will have him talking by the end of the week. Dead men file no reports.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Expect them to be better armed
      than the cartel. Expect them to fight. Expect civilians close by. Move out.'
    STR_LEAD_CARTEL_SUPPLIER_DESC: Somebody is arming the border cartel. Follow the guns, the planes and the money back to whoever it is.
    STR_EVENT_CARTEL_FLIGHT: CARTEL FLIGHT DEPARTING
    STR_EVENT_CARTEL_FLIGHT_DESCRIPTION: 'The flight the cartel boss gave us is in the air: a twin-engine cargo plane, running north without lights.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: Don''t shoot it down. Follow it.
      Wherever it lands is where they keep their stock.'
    STR_OP_SCARLETT_STASH_HOUSE: 'Operation: Quiet Courier'
    STR_OP_SCARLETT_STASH_HOUSE_DESC: Scarlett goes in alone, as a buyer, to the cartel's stash house. She'll bug a shipment or turn one of their couriers into our man. Either way we hear what they plan
      next.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}She'll be gone for days. Intel research slows while she's out, and if she's made, they'll hold her.
    STR_BRIEFING_ARMORED_CAR_TITLE: 'OPERATION: PAYROLL'
    STR_BRIEFING_ARMORED_CAR: 'HAWK: The cartel lost a fortune at the ranch and they want it back fast. Scarlett''s courier gave us the job: an armored car on a payroll run, hit at a gas station on the
      highway.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}They''ll come heavy and they''ll come quick. The money goes into a van, and the van goes for the county line. If it gets off the map, the cash is gone.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Local
      police will already be there, pinned down. Get them out alive. And I want the man running the crew in one piece. He knows where the money goes.'
    STR_BRIEFING_CARTEL_SAFEHOUSE_TITLE: 'OPERATION: COLD TRAIL'
    STR_BRIEFING_CARTEL_SAFEHOUSE: 'HAWK: They got away with the payroll. They didn''t get away clean. The van was dumped two counties over, and the trail ends at a farmhouse they''re using as a safehouse.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The
      money''s probably moved on. The paperwork usually doesn''t. Bring me anything with a number on it.'
    STR_BRIEFING_STASH_HOUSE_RESCUE_TITLE: 'OPERATION: BUYER BEWARE'
    STR_BRIEFING_STASH_HOUSE_RESCUE: 'HAWK: Scarlett''s cover is blown. The cartel are holding her at the stash house, and every day she''s in there she''s in more danger and we''re more exposed.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We
      go in now. Get her out first. Everything else is second.'
    STR_EVENT_CHOP_SHOP_INFORMANT: 'INFORMANT: A PRISONER AT THE CHOP SHOP'
    STR_EVENT_CHOP_SHOP_INFORMANT_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: My courier delivered more than he meant to. The cartel runs a chop shop outside the border town, and there''s a man in the back room who isn''t
      a customer.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Army driver. They took his vehicle on a test run and they''ve kept him alive to make it work. They''re running out of patience with him.'
    STR_BRIEFING_CHOP_SHOP_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SPARE PARTS'
    STR_BRIEFING_CHOP_SHOP: 'HAWK: Two months ago the Army lost a prototype on a test run near the border: a light attack vehicle, and the man driving it. Corporal Lance Steinberg. Everybody calls him Clutch.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}The
      cartel took both. The vehicle went for parts. Clutch they kept, because nobody else can make it run. He''s in a back room at their chop shop.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Get him out alive. Everything else in
      that yard is stolen, and most of it has a man with a pistol standing next to it. Don''t shoot the gas cans.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}If he''s half the driver his file says, I want him running our Motor Pool
      by the end of the month.'
    STR_EVENT_CLUTCH_MOVED: CLUTCH MOVED
    STR_EVENT_CLUTCH_MOVED_DESCRIPTION: 'We didn''t get him out. By the time the yard was quiet, the back room was empty and the cartel''s truck was gone.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: They''ll put him somewhere
      else and they''ll be more careful. Keep listening. We get one more chance at this.'
    STR_BRIEFING_CHOP_SHOP_2_TITLE: 'OPERATION: SECOND GEAR'
    STR_BRIEFING_CHOP_SHOP_2: 'HAWK: We found him again. The cartel moved Clutch to another of their garages, and this time they know we''re coming.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}More guards, fewer chances. Get in,
      get him, get out. There won''t be a third time.'
    STR_EVENT_CLUTCH_ESCAPED: CLUTCH WALKS IN
    STR_EVENT_CLUTCH_ESCAPED_DESCRIPTION: 'A filthy man in an Army jacket walks up to the gate of The Pit and asks for whoever''s in charge.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}CLUTCH: "Your rescue was lousy. Theirs was worse.
      I hot-wired the truck they were moving me in. Where''s the coffee?"'
    STR_CLUTCH_ARRIVAL: CLUTCH JOINS G.I. JOE
    STR_CLUTCH_ARRIVAL_DESCRIPTION: 'Corporal Lance "Clutch" Steinberg. Armor & Vehicles. He can head the Motor Pool.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}CLUTCH: "Two months I''m fixing their junk with a gun in my ear. Now:
      they still got my VAMP. It''s in a junkyard. I know which one. I want it back."'
    STR_BRIEFING_JUNKYARD_TITLE: 'OPERATION: REPO'
    STR_BRIEFING_JUNKYARD: 'HAWK: Clutch says the cartel never finished stripping his VAMP. It''s under a tarp in a shed at their junkyard, waiting for a buyer.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Take it back. It runs, it''s
      ours, and once Clutch has had it apart we can build more of them.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Watch the stacks. There are men up on those wrecks with a clear view of the whole yard, and a crusher in the middle
      that will flatten anybody who stands next to it when it starts.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}CLUTCH: "And nobody scratches the paint."'
    STR_EVENT_VAMP_RECOVERED: VAMP RECOVERED
    STR_EVENT_VAMP_RECOVERED_DESCRIPTION: 'The VAMP rolls into the Motor Pool on its own wheels, with Clutch at the wheel and one door missing.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}It''s ours, and Clutch has started on the
      drawings. Research: VAMP.'
    STR_EVENT_VAMP_LOST: VAMP GONE
    STR_EVENT_VAMP_LOST_DESCRIPTION: 'The shed was empty by the time we reached it. The cartel sold the VAMP before we could take it back.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}CLUTCH: "Fine. I''ll draw you a new one from memory.
      Give me a month." Research: VAMP, in about a month.'
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND: A VISITOR AT THE TRAINING ROOM
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND_DESCRIPTION: 'A Ranger sergeant in a balaclava inspects your new Training Room, says nothing for a full minute, then hands Hawk a sealed order.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: Beach
      Head. The Army sent him to tell me whether my people are any good. He''s offered to show us. On his range.'
    STR_BRIEFING_PROVING_GROUND_TITLE: 'OPERATION: PROVING GROUND'
    STR_BRIEFING_PROVING_GROUND: 'BEACH HEAD: Listen up, because I''m only saying this once. You think you''re soldiers. I think you''re tourists. Today we find out.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}My range. My men. Stun
      weapons only: nobody dies on my course, they just wish they had. Put my team on the ground, every last one, and you pass.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Lose, and I''ll be back next week. And the week after. Until
      you get it right.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Move like you mean it.'
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND_PASSED: BEACH HEAD JOINS G.I. JOE
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND_PASSED_DESCRIPTION: 'Sergeant Wayne "Beach Head" Sneeden. Infantry, Ranger, drill instructor. He can head Training & Recruiting and train up to six Joes in the Training Room.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}BEACH
      HEAD: "You''re slow, you''re sloppy and you talk too much. You''ll do. I''m staying."'
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND_FAILED: 'PROVING GROUND: FAILED'
    STR_EVENT_PROVING_GROUND_FAILED_DESCRIPTION: 'Your squad is carried off Beach Head''s range one stunned body at a time.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}BEACH HEAD: "Pathetic. Same time next week."'
    STR_EVENT_FACTORY_REACTIVATED: THE FACTORY IS RUNNING
    STR_EVENT_FACTORY_REACTIVATED_DESCRIPTION: 'The date on the production schedule came and went. The machine works in West Texas is lit up, the rail spur is busy, and there are guards on the gate.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK:
      We knew when. We didn''t get there. Cobra has a factory now, and the cartel''s next shipment won''t be pistols. We''ll have to hit it the hard way.'
    STR_EVENT_BLUDD_HIRED: A PRICE ON A JOE
    STR_EVENT_BLUDD_HIRED_DESCRIPTION: 'SCARLETT: Word from three different informants, all the same week. Cobra has hired a mercenary. Australian, ex-Foreign Legion, writes bad poetry. Major Sebastian
      Bludd.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}His job is one of ours: {JOE}. Cobra has seen enough of {JOE} to want him gone. Bludd will wait for him to travel. Every flight is a risk until this is settled.'
    STR_BRIEFING_BLUDD_AMBUSH_TITLE: AMBUSH
    STR_BRIEFING_BLUDD_AMBUSH: 'HAWK: Bludd hit the aircraft carrying {JOE}. It''s down, and his men are already moving on the wreck.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Get everyone out of that wreck before they do. Bludd
      doesn''t want the aircraft. He wants {JOE}.'
    STR_BRIEFING_BLUDD_RAID_TITLE: BLUDD AT THE GATE
    STR_BRIEFING_BLUDD_RAID: 'HAWK: {JOE} stayed home, so Bludd came to him. A small team is inside the wire at {BASE}.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}They''re not here to hold ground. They''re here for one man. Keep
      him alive and run them off.'
    STR_EVENT_BLUDD_CALLING_CARD: BLUDD WAS HERE
    STR_EVENT_BLUDD_CALLING_CARD_DESCRIPTION: 'Bludd got away. He left a card where we''d find it: a playing card, the ace of spades, with four lines of verse on the back promising to come back for {JOE}.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK:
      The poetry is terrible. The threat isn''t. Research: Bludd''s Calling Card.'
    STR_EVENT_DROME_STRIKE: THE DROME STRIKES
    STR_EVENT_DROME_STRIKE_DESCRIPTION: 'Radar has a wave of Firebats on it, and behind them Cobra transports, heading straight for {BASE}.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: We didn''t go to the Drome, so the Drome
      is coming to us. Everyone to battle stations. This is the one we''ve been building to.'
    STR_BRIEFING_DROME_STRIKE_TITLE: 'OPERATION: HOLD THE LINE'
    STR_BRIEFING_DROME_STRIKE: 'HAWK: Cobra''s Terror Drome has sent everything it has at {BASE}. Troops, armour, aircraft overhead.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Hold the base. Take prisoners if you can, pick up their
      weapons when it''s over. I want to know who''s been arming these people.'
    STR_BRIEFING_ROUTINE_SIGHTING_TITLE: 'OPERATION: ROUTINE PATROL'
    STR_BRIEFING_ROUTINE_SIGHTING: 'HAWK: Local police report armed men in a Cobra-style van moving through the area. Probably a supply run. Probably nothing.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Go and take a look. If it''s
      Cobra, bring me a prisoner. If it isn''t, be home for dinner.'
    STR_EVENT_AMBUSH: AMBUSH!
    STR_EVENT_AMBUSH_DESCRIPTION: It was a trap. Cobra troops are coming out of every building on one side of the street. Twenty of them, at least.
    STR_EVENT_SLAUGHTER_ARRIVES: SOMETHING BIG IS COMING
    STR_EVENT_SLAUGHTER_ARRIVES_DESCRIPTION: 'An engine roars behind the Cobra line. A small, ugly, very angry tank comes through a fence, and a man in a campaign hat is standing in the hatch.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SGT.
      SLAUGHTER: "Cobra! You picked the wrong street, the wrong day and the wrong sergeant! Joes, keep your heads down and watch how it''s done!"'
    STR_EVENT_SLAUGHTER_JOINS: SGT. SLAUGHTER JOINS G.I. JOE
    STR_EVENT_SLAUGHTER_JOINS_DESCRIPTION: 'Sergeant Slaughter. Drill instructor, Command. He can head Training & Recruiting, and his Triple T tank comes with him.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}SGT. SLAUGHTER: "I''ve
      been watching your outfit, Hawk. Good people. Soft. I''m going to fix that. Where do I sign?"'
    STR_EVENT_PIT_ATTACK: THE PIT IS UNDER ATTACK
    STR_EVENT_PIT_ATTACK_DESCRIPTION: 'Cobra has found us. Trucks and troops are at the fence, and they know exactly where the lift shed is.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: Everyone who can carry a rifle, topside.
      We hold the yard and this ends here.'
    STR_EVENT_PIT_BREACHED: COBRA IS IN THE PIT
    STR_EVENT_PIT_BREACHED_DESCRIPTION: They took the yard. Cobra is coming down the lift. Fall back to the rooms and make them pay for every corridor.
    STR_PIT_EVACUATE: EVACUATE
    STR_PIT_EVACUATE_DESCRIPTION: Get everyone to the lift and the escape hatch. Whatever we leave behind, Cobra gets.
    STR_PIT_SELF_DESTRUCT: SELF-DESTRUCT
    STR_PIT_SELF_DESTRUCT_DESCRIPTION: Charges set. Five turns. Get out, or stay and hold them while it counts down. Anyone still inside when it blows will be taken.
    STR_EVENT_PIT_DESTROYED: THE PIT IS GONE
    STR_EVENT_PIT_DESTROYED_DESCRIPTION: 'The ground jumped and the lift shed folded into the hole. Cobra took nothing out of The Pit but its own dead.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: We start again. We''ve done
      it before.'
    STR_EVENT_PIT_HELD: COBRA HOLDS THE PIT
    STR_EVENT_PIT_HELD_DESCRIPTION: 'We got out. Cobra has The Pit: our rooms, our labs, our files. Every week they''re in there, they learn more about us.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK: We know exactly where it
      is. When we''re ready, we take it back.'
    STR_EVENT_NEW_HQ: NEW HEADQUARTERS
    STR_EVENT_NEW_HQ_DESCRIPTION: Command moves to {BASE}. Washington is asking hard questions.
    STR_BRIEFING_RETAKE_PIT_TITLE: 'OPERATION: HOMECOMING'
    STR_BRIEFING_RETAKE_PIT: 'HAWK: We built every room in that hole. We know every corridor, every blind corner and every vent better than the people sitting in it.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Go home. Throw them
      out. Try not to break anything we''ll need.'
    STR_EVENT_FIRST_INTERCEPT: SMUGGLER OVER THE BORDER
    STR_EVENT_FIRST_INTERCEPT_DESCRIPTION: 'Border radar has a twin-engine plane coming north low and without lights. Customs say guns, and nobody else is close enough to stop it.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}HAWK:
      Ace, it''s yours. Force it down. I want the plane, the guns and the pilot.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}ACE: "Finally. Somebody around here who needs a pilot."'
    STR_TIP_AIR_TURN: Your Skystriker's gun only fires forward. Turn to put the target inside the bright arc in front of you before you shoot.
    STR_TIP_AIR_DECKS: The fight has four decks, low to high. Climbing costs time units, diving gains them. A plane on another deck can't be hit by guns.
    STR_TIP_AIR_FIRE: Fire when the target is in your arc and on your deck. The closer you are, the more of the burst hits.
    STR_TIP_AIR_MISSILES: Missiles lock on from further away and hit hard, but you carry only two. Save them for something that shoots back.
    STR_TIP_AIR_EDGE: A plane that reaches its edge of the map gets away. Get between it and its edge, or bring it down before it gets there.
    STR_TIP_SKIP: SKIP TIPS
    STR_EVENT_COBRA_BROADCAST: COBRA SPEAKS
    STR_EVENT_COBRA_BROADCAST_DESCRIPTION: 'Every television and radio station in the free world loses its signal for ninety seconds. When the picture returns, a man in a blue hood stands in front of a
      banner bearing a coiled snake.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}"People of the world. You have been governed by the weak, defended by the timid, and lied to by both. That ends now. My name does not matter. My organisation
      does. We are COBRA.{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}We are already in your cities, your factories and your banks. Governments that cooperate will find us generous. Governments that resist will learn what we are
      named for. This is your only warning. COBRA!"{NEWLINE}{NEWLINE}Breaker has the recording. The signal was relayed, and every relay leaves a trace. Research: Trace the Broadcast.'
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_A1: West Texas. The date on the schedule.
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_A2: The dust sheets come off. The machines still work.
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_A3: Under the floor, something else was never switched off.
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_A4: By morning the first crates are on the rails. Cobra is in the arms business.
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_B1: West Texas. The date on the schedule.
    STR_CUT_FACTORY_B2: Cobra's trucks find the gates chained and the lines wrecked. They turn around. Somewhere, someone takes note of who did it.
    STR_CUT_DROME_A1: The plans were real.
    STR_CUT_DROME_B1: No plans. Just a reconnaissance photograph, and a lot of anti-aircraft fire.
    STR_CUT_DROME_2: Cobra's first Terror Drome.
    STR_CUT_DROME_3: Its own air wing. Its own garrison. Its own region to command.
    STR_CUT_DROME_4: Every depot, every cell, every crate of rifles was building toward this.
    STR_CUT_CLOSE_A1: The first Terror Drome burns. Cobra Commander is not among the prisoners.
    STR_CUT_CLOSE_B1: The first Terror Drome still stands. G.I. Joe will be back.
    STR_CUT_CLOSE_2: 'Under the Cobra paint, a maker''s mark: M.A.R.S.'
    STR_CUT_CLOSE_3: Somewhere far from Texas, someone is watching the footage.
    STR_CUT_CLOSE_4: He has seen enough. He is interested.
- type: en-GB
  strings: *id001
